  "notes": "Most genitives answer 'whose?' or 'of what whole?'. Two others are worth flagging: description (always with an adjective — vir magnae virtūtis) and the genitive that certain adjectives simply require (plēnus, cupidus, perītus). English 'of' is a rough guide but not a reliable one.",
